5-03-19T09:35:35Z"},"comments":4,"created_at":"2024-10-20T06:45:23Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T10:22:36Z","closed_at":"2024-10-25T02:41:44Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98357","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98357","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98357.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98357.patch","merged_at":"2024-10-25T02:41:44Z"},"body":"Add valid base check for `String::num_int64` and `String::num_uint64` to ensure that the `base` parameter is within the valid range [2, 36]. Previously, `String::num_uint64` conversion with base 0 or 1 caused Godot to crash, instead of returning an error. \r\n\r\nFixes #98347 \r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n`String::num_int64`\r\n  - [x] base < 2 returns an empty string and prints an error message\r\n  - [x] base > 36 returns an empty string and prints an error message \r\n\r\n`String::num_uint64`\r\n  - [x] no previous unit tests on `num_uint64` - added basic functionality tests \r\n  - [x] base < 2 returns an empty string and prints an error message\r\n  - [x] base > 36 returns an empty string and prints an error message \r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_ur